  "scenes": [
    {
      "heading": "Plants Eat Sunlight",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "teacher",
          "text": "What if I told you every breath you take was made by a leaf?",
          "pose": "wave",
          "listener_pose": "shocked",
          "shots": [
            {
              "kind": "title",
              "cue": "",
              "title": "",
              "text": "Every breath was made by a leaf",
              "emphasis": "leaf",
              "icon": "leaf",
              "label": "",
              "value": "",
              "items": []
            }
          ],
          "audio": "audio/s00_l00.wav",
          "duration": 2.5565,
          "audio_start": 0.38045835
        },
        {
          "speaker": "student",
          "text": "Wait, what? Leaves make air?",
          "pose": "shocked",
          "listener_pose": "excited",
          "shots": [
            {
              "kind": "talk",
              "cue": "",
              "title": "",
              "text": "Leaves make AIR?!",
              "emphasis": "",
              "icon": "leaf",
              "label": "",
              "value": "",
              "items": []
            }
          ],
          "audio": "audio/s00_l01.wav",
          "duration": 1.4007083,
          "audio_start": 0.18058333
        },
        {
          "speaker": "teacher",
          "text": "Yep. It's called photosynthesis. Plants turn light, water and carbon dioxide into sugar and oxygen.",
          "pose": "explain",
          "listener_pose": "think",
          "shots": [
            {
              "kind": "definition",
              "cue": "",
              "title": "Photosynthesis",
              "text": "How plants turn light energy into chemical energy stored in sugar.",
              "emphasis": "",
              "icon": "sun",
              "label": "",
              "value": "",
              "items": []
            },
            {
              "kind": "flow",
              "cue": "light",
              "title": "The recipe",
              "text": "",
              "emphasis": "",
              "icon": "",
              "label": "",
              "value": "",
              "items": [
                {
                  "label": "Light",
                  "icon": "sun",
                  "note": ""
                },
                {
                  "label": "Water",
                  "icon": "water",
                  "note": ""
                },
                {
                  "label": "Carbon dioxide",
                  "icon": "cloud",
                  "note": ""
                },
                {
                  "label": "Sugar",
                  "icon": "apple",
                  "note": ""
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "audio": "audio/s00_l02.wav",
          "duration": 4.979083,
          "audio_start": 0.181
        },
        {
          "speaker": "teacher",
          "text": "Here's the whole thing as one equation.",
          "pose": "point",
          "listener_pose": "think",
          "shots": [
            {
              "kind": "formula",
              "cue": "",
              "title": "The equation",
              "text": "6 CO2 + 6 H2O → C6H12O6 + 6 O2",
              "emphasis": "",
              "icon": "",
              "label": "carbon dioxide plus water makes glucose plus oxygen",
              "value": "",
              "items": []
            }
          ],
          "audio": "audio/s00_l03.wav",
          "duration": 1.5022917,
          "audio_start": 0.24400002
        }
      ],
      "quiz": {
        "question": "What gas do plants release?",
        "choices": [
          "Carbon dioxide",
          "Oxygen",
          "Nitrogen"
        ],
        "answer_index": 1,
        "explanation": "Oxygen is the by-product of splitting water."
      }
    },
    {
      "heading": "Inside the Chloroplast",
      "lines": [
        {
          "speaker": "teacher",
          "text": "All of this happens inside tiny green machines called chloroplasts.",
          "pose": "point",
          "listener_pose": "idle",
          "shots": [
            {
              "kind": "icon",
              "cue": "",
              "title": "",
              "text": "a tiny green solar panel",
              "emphasis": "",
              "icon": "cell",
              "label": "Chloroplast",
              "value": "",
              "items": []
            }
          ],
          "audio": "audio/s01_l00.wav",
          "duration": 3.4334166,
          "audio_start": 0.23087502
        },
        {
          "speaker": "teacher",
          "text": "There are two stages. The light reactions, and the Calvin cycle.",
          "pose": "explain",
          "listener_pose": "think",
          "shots": [
            {
              "kind": "compare",
              "cue": "",
              "title": "",
              "text": "",
              "emphasis": "",
              "icon": "",
              "label": "",
              "value": "",
              "items": [
                {
                  "label": "Light reactions",
                  "icon": "sun",
                  "note": "make ATP and oxygen"
                },
                {
                  "label": "Calvin cycle",
                  "icon": "gear",
                  "note": "builds sugar"
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "audio": "audio/s01_l01.wav",
          "duration": 3.2055833,
          "audio_start": 0.16833332
        },
        {
          "speaker": "student",
          "text": "So plants get their energy from the soil, right?",
          "pose": "confused",
          "listener_pose": "facepalm",
          "shots": [
            {
              "kind": "myth",
              "cue": "",
              "title": "Plants get their food from the soil",
              "text": "Plants make their own food from light and air",
              "emphasis": "",
              "icon": "",
              "label": "",
              "value": "",
              "items": []
            }
          ],
          "audio": "audio/s01_l02.wav",
          "duration": 2.2852914,
          "audio_start": 0.14191666
        },
        {
          "speaker": "teacher",
          "text": "Nope! The Calvin cycle grabs carbon, fixes it, reduces it, and regenerates the starter molecule.",
          "pose": "explain",
          "listener_pose": "think",
          "shots": [
            {
              "kind": "cycle",
              "cue": "",
              "title": "Calvin cycle",
              "text": "",
              "emphasis": "",
              "icon": "",
              "label": "",
              "value": "",
              "items": [
                {
                  "label": "Carbon",
                  "icon": "cloud",
                  "note": ""
                },
                {
                  "label": "Fixes",
                  "icon": "link",
                  "note": ""
                },
                {
                  "label": "Reduces",
                  "icon": "battery",
                  "note": ""
                },
                {
                  "label": "Regenerates",
                  "icon": "recycle",
                  "note": ""
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          "audio": "audio/s01_l03.wav",
          "duration": 4.792375,
          "audio_start": 0.174
        },
        {
          "speaker": "teacher",
          "text": "Fun fact: plants capture about one hundred and thirty terawatts of energy.",
          "pose": "excited",
          "listener_pose": "shocked",
          "shots": [
            {
              "kind": "number",
              "cue": "",
              "title": "",
              "text": "of sunlight captured by plants every second",
              "emphasis": "",
              "icon": "lightning",
              "label": "",
              "value": "130 TW",
              "items": []
            }
          ],
          "audio": "audio/s01_l04.wav",
          "duration": 3.4799998,
          "audio_start": 0.38333336
        }
      ]
    },
